Interview Questions
1. What is the difference between git add and git commit?
git add stages changes.
git commit records the staged changes in the local repository.
2. What is the difference between git diff and git diff --staged?
git diff shows unstaged changes.
git diff --staged shows staged changes that will be committed.
3. What does git clean do?

It removes untracked files from the working directory. Use git clean -n first to preview what will be deleted.

4. When would you use git restore?

To discard local uncommitted changes or to unstage files using git restore --staged.

5. What is the safest way to check the current repository status?
git status
